CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Sustain Operational Use Time (OUT) of 99.00% or better. OUT is defined as the percentage of time the NCEP Production Suite (NPS) can run on the WCOSS. OUT is determined by considering all WCOSS resources in which a subset of this total resource is necessary to execute the entire NPS. The NPS executes on either the Primary or Backup WCOSS.", ID:"2485", Measurement_category:"216-Technology - Effectiveness", Metric_results:"Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:4710});
CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Sustain Development Use Time (DUT) of 99.00% or better. DUT is defined as the percentage of time development jobs can run on the WCOSS. DUT is determined by considering all WCOSS resources minus the resources necessary to execute the entire NCEP Production Suite (NPS). The Transition to Operations (T2O) executes within the DUT and the T2O will execute on the Primary and Backup WCOSS.", ID:"2486", Measurement_category:"111-Customer Results - Customer Benefit", Metric_results:"Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:4711});
CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Increase capability X-Factor of operational supercomputer. The new WCOSS contracts include built-in requirements to provide contractual high performance computing capability increases with steady state funds. The X-Factor may also be increased by exercising growth options if funding is made available. NOAA modeling plans rely heavily on these built-in capability increases for model improvements during the WCOSS upgrade life-cycle.", ID:"2487", Measurement_category:"211-Technology - Technology Costs", Metric_results:"Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:4712});
CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Sustain System Availability of 99% or better.  System Availability is the percentage of time the WCOSS was available to run operational (NPS) and development (T2O) jobs. System Availability is computed as the ratio of total processor minutes available for running the operational and development suites to the total processor minutes available each month.", ID:"2488", Measurement_category:"215-Technology - Reliability and Availability", Metric_results:"Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:4713});
