CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Overage Reparables.  Reparables are critical repair parts that can be repaired at a fraction of the original cost.  When a reparable item is needed to make equipment mission capable it is ordered from the servicing supply support activity.  The requiring activity must return the unserviceable like item.  The customer has 10 days to return the like unserviceable item after which point it becomes OVERAGE.  Monitoring the 10 day regulatory policy promotes mission readiness and fiscal prudence.", ID:"4287", Measurement_category:"103-Mission and Business Results - Management of Government Resources", Metric_results:"Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:4999});
CREATE (:Investment:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Enhancement_spend_$m:254.908, Identifier:"007-000005070", Investment_type:"Major", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:5000});
CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Readiness Driver Satisfaction.  This metric measures the degree to which Maintenance Significant Parts (MSP) were provided to the customer upon demand in order to execute its maintenance mission.", ID:"4288", Measurement_category:"113-Customer Results - Timeliness and Responsiveness", Metric_results:"Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:5001});
CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Overdue Deliveries with Dues-Out.  The Supply Support Activity provides repair parts and supplies. Its tailored package of stocks must be replenished.  Tracking inbound shipments is key to maintaining a functioning level of stocks.  OVERDUE inbound shipments are researched to avoid stock shortages, which may degrade the mission.  An arbitrary number (45 days) used to define OVERDUE. GCSS-Army increased the efficiency of this process by calculating average delivery time by individual material.", ID:"4289", Measurement_category:"206-Process and Activities - Management and Innovation", Metric_results:"Not Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:5002});
CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Customer Reconciliation.  This process is intended to resolve discrepancies between customer and SSA records.  Every customer order that is not on the SSA record is usually reordered at cost.  When this cost is extrapolated across the Army, Reserve and National Guard, the recurring cost of reordering becomes significant.", ID:"4290", Measurement_category:"213-Technology - Efficiency", Metric_results:"Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:5003});
CREATE (:Metric:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Description:"Readiness Driver Fill Rate.  This metric measures the breadth (how many) and the depth (how much of each) of an Authorized Stockage List (ASL).  The ASL is the stock package an SSA uses to support its customer base.  The ASL contains critical and non critical parts and supplies.  This metric focuses on the performance of the Maintenance Significant Parts known as Readiness Drivers.  The current direction is to stock more Readiness Driver and less non-critical items.", ID:"4291", Measurement_category:"216-Technology - Effectiveness", Metric_results:"Met", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:5004});
