CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_duration:"252 days", Actual_start_delay:"0 days", Id:"1343", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"252 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2011-02-14", description:"Develop new software so the CPSTR system is capable of printing the newly redesigned EAD card.", name:"CPSTR Relase 1.1", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"0.419", status:"Completed - Closed", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:15034});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_start_delay:"0 days", Id:"1344", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"1826 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2007-03-01", description:"USCIS has a requirement to obtain specially designed dye sublimation and laser engaveable optical card (with or without RFID chip inlays) consumables materials including card stock, holograms, and laminates necessary for production of secure identification cards required to produce the Permanent Resident Cards (PRCs). The PRC card consumables contain a number of very specific custom-designed visual and structure security features, more specifically, colors and multi-layered security features imbedded in the card structure, which make the card counterfeit resistant.  This FP/IDIQ contract allows expeditious delivery of optical PRC card stock and related consumables in accordance with the Statement of Work and technical specifications, and the delivery schedule and requirements included in the delivery orders.  In addition, the Contractor is required to maintain a process for responding to government corrective action requests arising from problems in faulty card production issues originating with the contractor. The process is designed to foster quick determination of the origination of the problem and equally quick determination and implementation of a solution, and if necessary, provide replacements for faulty card consumables as part of corrective action/resolution process.  The contractor performance rating is primarily based on their ability to deliver quality products on time and timely resolution of all issues reported through the corrective action process.", name:"Optical Card Consumables Contract", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"7.2", status:"In-progress", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:15035});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_start_delay:"0 days", Id:"1345", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"1825 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2009-04-10", description:"USCIS has a requirement to obtain specially designed non-optical dye sublimation and laser engraveable card consumables materials including card stock, holograms, and laminates necessary for production of secure identification cards required to produce the Employment Authorization Documents (EADs). The EAD card consumables contain a number of very specific custom-designed visual and structure security features, more specifically, colors and multi-layered security features imbedded in the card structure, which make the card counterfeit resistant.  This FP/IDIQ contract allows expeditious delivery of non-optical EAD card stock and related consumables in accordance with the Statement of Work and technical specifications, and the delivery schedule and requirements included in the delivery orders.  In addition, the Contractor is required to maintain a process for responding to government corrective action requests arising from problems in faulty card production issues originating with the contractor. The process is designed to foster quick determination of the origination of the problem and equally quick determination and implementation of a solution, and if necessary, provide replacements for faulty card consumables as part of corrective action/resolution process.  The contractor performance rating is primarily based on their ability to deliver quality products on time and timely resolution of all issues reported through the corrective action process.", name:"Non-Optical Card Consumables Contract", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"2.3", status:"In-progress", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:15036});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_start_delay:"-1 days", Id:"1346", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"1825 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2008-01-08", description:"The system must be capable of personalizing at least 5.7 million cards Optical Memory Cards with RFID chips per year, and 1.9 million Non-optical cards per year. The Government is assuming a system lifecycle of at least eight years. The system is designed to provide easy access to components requiring routine or frequent maintenance or adjustment. The Contractor will maintain the system, and has a requirement that components be capable of being repaired or replaced such that no component failure would lead to a shutdown lasting longer than 48 hours.", name:"Card Personalization System Technology Refreshment (CPSTR)", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"2.4", status:"In-progress", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:15037});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_start_delay:"0 days", Id:"1347", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"1095 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2010-07-06", description:"The IDP Division produces secure document products that are mission critical to Department of Homeland Security (DHS). The contractor provides the labor to perform inventory control, production staging, card and/or document personalization, quality control, shipping, and destruction of excess materials incident to the production process. The vendor maintains 100% accountability for all consumables from their receipt on site throughout the personalization process and completes audit traceability from receipt of electronic orders to posting of results in USCIS information systems. The Contractor must produce all Optical and Non-Optical cards within 72 hours of receiving the card orders. All Transportation Worker Identification Credentials (TWIC) and Travel Document booklets must be produced within 48 hours of receiving the order. In addition to card production, the Contractor performs program management, transition support, operations in support of installation and testing, system migration support, and system up-grade support.", name:"Card Operations Services", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"2.5", status:"In-progress", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:15038});
