CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_start_delay:"26 days", Id:"11542", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"164 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2012-04-19", description:"FedDebt NG 2 will continue to iteratively build the system based on goals identified in FedDebt NG 1", name:"FedDebt NG 2", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"1.383", status:"In-progress", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:18035});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_duration:"219 days", Actual_start_delay:"0 days", Id:"11543", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"200 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2011-10-01", description:"TOP NG Release 3:Although a continuation of the project, Release 3, albiet a continuation of the project, will continue to focus on incrementally building the solution.  It is anticipated that the Inception & Elaboration Phases will be shorter, but is truly dependent on newly identified risks and Stakeholder Needs.  Agile Inception Phase:  1-2 Iterations -  Confirm Objectives and Scope of the project and bring the newly identified Business Risks under control.  The focus of the team is on any new Stakeholders to elicit their Needs & define measurable Desired outcomes including engaging the previously.  The team will focus on the refining the Business Priority and risks list reviews for newly identified risks to the successful delivery and ultimately the basic viability of the project, especially as it relates to the underlying proven solution & technical architecture.  Demonstration of working software, Customer Inspection and Acceptance will occur at the end of each iteration.  Before moving to the next phase, the team will plan and organize the content of the 3 planned software releases.  Next, the team will move into the Elaboration Phase.  TOP NG Release 3: Agile Elaboration Phase:  1-2 Iterations -  Stabilize the product plans and bring the Architectural and Technical Risks under control.The team will start to prove the candidate solution architecture by building the riskiest elements to prove the viability of the candidate architecture to support the key Stakeholder Needs.  Performed by iteratively building Use Case scenarios with highest risk exposure to the candidate architecture to incrementally prove & build elements of the solution architecture.  Disciplines of Requirements, Analysis & Design, Coding & QA Testing will be executed to encompass identified Use Case scenarios.  Demonstration of working software, Customer Inspection and Acceptance will occur at the end of each iteration.  Phase usually ends when all of the highest risks that are architecturally significant have been attacked, denoting a proven candidate architecture.", name:"TOP NG 5", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"1.189", status:"Completed - Closed", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:18036});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_start_delay:"19 days", Id:"11544", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"164 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2012-04-19", description:"TOP NG Release 3: Agile Construction Phase:  4-6 Iterations -  Build the product, bring the logistical, project execution risks under control.The team will continue to incrementally build functional slices for Release 1 of the TOP NG.  Disciplines of Requirements, Analysis & Design, Coding & QA Testing will be executed to encompass identified Use Case scenarios.  Demonstration of working software, Customer Inspection and Acceptance will occur at the end of each iteration.  Phase usually ends when all execution risks have been attacked.TOP NG Release 3: Agile Transition Phase: 1-2 Iterations: Deliver the product, conduct business change management, transition ownership to the application maintenance team and bring the roll-out risks under control.", name:"TOP NG 6", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"1.209", status:"In-progress", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:18037});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_duration:"200 days", Actual_start_delay:"0 days", Id:"11545", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"200 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2011-10-01", description:"Project Management Activities:1. Establish Backlog for Product, Project & Iteration- define backlog items- agree to backlog item Business Priority- assess backlog item Risk- establish prioritized backlog- estimate backlog item effort2. Groom Backlog with Customer Representatives - ongoing basis- define new backlog items- agree to new backlog item Business Priority- assess new backlog item Risk- establish prioritized backlog3. Establish & Maintain Project Charter- define encompassing desired outcomes of the key business stakeholder - define stakeholder problems based on root cause analysis- define characteristics of a successful solution related to each stakeholder problem- define desired outcomes and define measures of a successful solution for each desired outcome.4. Daily Standups- coordinate daily stand-ups within each iteration- facilitate resolution of blocked tasks for team members5. Iteration Planning & Assessment- coordinate iteration planning- define objectives, measurements traced to risks to bring under control- coordinate iteration assessment- coordinate 360 degree retrospective- coordinate Iteration Review with Project Sponsor, Key Stakeholders, Project Network & TOP NG team.", name:"PM Support Activity", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"0.821", status:"Completed - Closed", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:18038});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_start_delay:"0 days", Id:"11546", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"164 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2012-04-19", description:"TBD", name:"PM Support Activity 2", output_type:"Key Deliverable", planned_Costs:"0.832", status:"In-progress", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:18039});
CREATE (:Activity:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL` {Actual_start_delay:"0 days", Id:"11559", No_Child_Activity:"1", Planned_Duration:"352 days", Start_Date_Planned:"2011-10-01", description:"This activity provides for the design, development and implementation of e Transcripts which is an application which will will allow taxpayers to request any of the following documents; a transcript of their account for a particular tax year, a form 4506, which they may fill out and return to the IRS in order to receive a photocopy of their return, or a transcript of their return for a particular tax year.  The taxpayer will also have the choice to receive both a transcript of their account and a transcript of their return for a particular tax year.  In order to receive the document, the address the IRS has on file for the taxpayer must match the address entered by the taxpayer.  Specifically, the street address, rural route number, or post office box number will be verified to ensure that the requested document is sent to the correct residence.", name:"Design,  Development and implementation of eTranscripts ", output_type:"Usable Functionality", planned_Costs:"1.15", status:"In-progress", `UNIQUE IMPORT ID`:18040});
